Logic of the mux-demux above is as follows:

The Mux switches a single port between two ports.
As in, 1A can go to 1B1 or 1B2. 
Output enable is tied to GND, thus 1 of 2 connections always happen.
 SELECT (S pin) high ties common to 2nd port (1A -> 1B2).

Wiring is 
	1A is SCLK of flash
		1B1 SCLK from I2C to SPI bridge
		1B2 SCLK from FPGA
	2A is MOSI of flash
		2B1 mosi of bridge
		2B2 mosi of fpga

	3A MISO of flash
		3B1 miso IS602B
		3B2 miso fpga

	4A chip select of flash
		4B1 !SS0 (slv sel 0) of bridge
		4B2 slv select of fpga

MUX selection controlled thru SPI SS1 of I2C-SPI bridge. Which can be used as a GPIO (?) directly.
Thus using SS1, a takeover of the flash can be done from the STM. Then, SS0 can be used to read-write flash memory.



